<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈdʒu.mu.ɑ">Jumu'ah</phoneme> briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">10042026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Iran's new Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei has declared the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="streɪt əv hɔrˈmuːz">Strait of Hormuz</phoneme> has entered what he called a new phase, broadcasting the message on state television just hours before ceasefire talks opened in Washington.</s> <s>The strait carries a fifth of the world's oil and hasn't moved commercial tankers in a month — the largest supply disruption in recorded history.</s> <s>Whether Tehran's signaling conditional reopening or tightening its grip as leverage will define what emerges from those talks.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Within hours of signing the Iran ceasefire, Israel launched a hundred strikes on Lebanon, killing over two hundred people and wounding more than a thousand in Beirut — insisting the truce excluded Lebanese territory.</s> <s>By late March, Israel had expended a hundred and twenty-two of its hundred and fifty Arrow interceptor missiles, each costing millions and taking months to replace, with US Navy ships now filling the defensive gap.</s> <s>Finance Minister Smotrich used the same week to announce three territories Israel intends to annex, including parts of Lebanon and Syria.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>India's Election Commission deleted eight point nine million voters from West Bengal's rolls, and the pattern reveals a troubling skew.</s> <s>Muslim-majority constituencies represent twenty-three percent of the state's electorate but absorbed over forty percent of the deletions — a ratio six times the statistical baseline.</s> <s>Final rolls aren't set, with more than twenty-two thousand names still under adjudication, raising sharp questions about whether the world's largest democracy is selectively shrinking its own franchise.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Police in Caracas fired tear gas at pensioners and public sector workers marching toward the presidential palace.</s> <s>Venezuela's minimum wage sits at a hundred and thirty bolivars — under thirty American cents a month — unchanged as inflation devours what little purchasing power remains.</s> <s>Acting President Rodríguez promised a raise from May first without specifying the amount, continuing a pattern of vague pledges that keeps workers on the streets.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Three health workers were shot dead at a health centre and private clinic in Ethiopia's Amhara region on April second, caught between federal and regional forces fighting across North Gojjam.</s> <s>The <sub alias="World Health Organization">WHO</sub> demanded an impartial investigation, calling attacks on medical personnel a violation of protections that even wars are supposed to respect.</s> <s>No party has claimed responsibility, and the conflict continues to choke healthcare access across the region.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>American airstrikes killed seven Iraqi state soldiers from the Popular Mobilization Forces, hitting their base in Anbar province five times on March twenty-fifth.</s> <s>The PMF are formally incorporated into Iraq's military under Baghdad's command, which means the US struck an ally's own armed forces.</s> <s>Baghdad hasn't lodged a formal protest, and whether the strikes resume remains unresolved.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Freedom of information requests show BAE Systems sits on fifty-three university advisory committees across twenty-one British universities, alongside defence contractors Leonardo and Thales.</s> <s>These firms help shape strategic direction for academic departments, influencing what students learn and what research gets funded.</s> <s>No law governs arms industry access to university curricula, and none of the twenty-one institutions has disclosed what changed.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Sixty nations have declared energy emergencies since the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="streɪt əv hɔrˈmuːz">Strait of Hormuz</phoneme> closure, deploying a hundred and eighty-five policies that range from fuel tax cuts to emergency coal restarts.</s> <s>The <sub alias="International Monetary Fund">IMF</sub> now expects twenty to fifty billion dollars in emergency balance-of-payments demand, warning that forty-five million people face food insecurity from the price surge alone.</s> <s>Even with a ceasefire, God willing, damaged port and pipeline infrastructure means the energy crisis will outlast the conflict that caused it.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Singapore — where Lee Kuan Yew once credited air conditioning with building a modern nation — is now rationing it.</s> <s>The city-state imports every unit of energy it consumes, and surging fuel costs from the Hormuz closure have forced a twenty-five degree cap on office cooling.</s> <s>If the strait stays shut much longer, further restrictions will follow — a sobering prospect for a tropical metropolis built entirely on climate control.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Conflict gold looted by Sudan's Rapid Support Forces has reached Volkswagen's supply chain.</s> <s>The RSF seized Sudan's national gold refinery in May twenty twenty-three, routing an estimated hundred and fifty million dollars in stolen gold through Dubai into global markets.</s> <s>Volkswagen hasn't confirmed whether it's suspended purchases — and OECD due-diligence rules exist precisely to stop conflict minerals from ending up in consumer products.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>At least twenty-four chimpanzees have been killed in what scientists are calling a civil war within Uganda's Ngogo community — the largest wild chimp group ever studied, at two hundred individuals.</s> <s>The group fractured in twenty fifteen, and former allies now stage lethal raids against each other in the first documented case of decade-long coalition warfare among non-human primates.</s> <s>Researchers say the killing is strategic, not random, and the war shows no sign of ending.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Chinese researchers have developed an improved CRISPR gene-editing system to treat beta-thalassaemia — a hereditary blood disorder that disproportionately affects South Asian and Middle Eastern populations.</s> <s>The new technique produces fewer off-target DNA cuts than earlier methods, precisely targeting the faulty hemoglobin gene that causes the disease.</s> <s>Clinical data supports regulatory review, but whether the treatment reaches the communities who carry the heaviest burden of this disease remains the harder question.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Emperor penguins have been reclassified as endangered after three consecutive record lows in Antarctic sea ice caused colony-wide breeding failures.</s> <s>The species needs stable ice for nine months to raise its young — a biological requirement that a warming climate is steadily erasing.</s> <s>Current projections show the population of two hundred and fifty-six thousand breeding pairs could fall by up to fifty-nine percent over three generations.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Treasury Secretary Bessent and Fed Chair Powell convened five major bank CEOs after Anthropic's AI model Mythos demonstrated it could discover and weaponize zero-day vulnerabilities in financial infrastructure.</s> <s>Anthropic sells the model under a programme called Project Glasswing, and the Pentagon's flagged it as a supply-chain risk to the banking system.</s> <s>When the Treasury Secretary and the Fed Chair call an emergency meeting with bank chiefs, the threat to financial infrastructure isn't theoretical — it's arrived.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Seven hundred and ninety-five Hungarian government passwords are circulating online, spanning twelve of the country's thirteen ministries.</s> <s>Bellingcat identified leaked credentials belonging to a military officer responsible for information security and a counter-terrorism coordinator — the very people charged with preventing this kind of breach.</s> <s>Hungary votes Sunday on Orbán's fifth term, and Russian intelligence services have historically exploited compromised government credentials during election periods.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Russia's military drone force is scaling to a hundred and sixty-five thousand five hundred troops by year's end — a sixty percent increase that would make it larger than most national armies.</s> <s>Ukrainian commander Syrskyi disclosed the figure, adding that Ukraine's own drone units killed more Russian soldiers from December to March than Moscow recruited in the same period.</s> <s>The air war has become a contest of industrial production as much as battlefield tactics.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈdʒu.mu.ɑ">Jumu'ah</phoneme> briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>